ecíficos. Además, no se puede asegurar que no haya sido un proceso conforme con las normas aplicables.\nQué se puede revisar: Es importante comprobar si los contratos adjudicados en diciembre se distribuyen de forma equitativa entre los adjudicatarios. También se puede analizar si el adjudicatario A, que tiene la mayor cantidad de contratos cerca del límite, repite la misma tarea o si se trata de diferentes necesidades. Un análisis detallado de los contratos [1] y [2] podría revelar si se han utilizado los mismos proveedores o si se han tenido en cuenta criterios distintos.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 43 minor contracts for works above 37,500 and up to 40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 1.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 35.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 15.2 to 103.0. December accounts for 5% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 4% of all its works contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 22 different awardees. Contract [1], for 39,752.22 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the limit does not mean that any of them were improperly awarded. It could reflect normal market pricing, budget constraints, or the need for multiple smaller contracts to meet specific requirements.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the specific reasons for the amount. Also, review the distribution of contracts across different awardees to identify if any single provider was awarded multiple contracts for similar services. Look for patterns in the timing of awards, especially in December, to understand if there's a seasonal trend.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["0zxLOk0x1fSExvMJXBMHHQ%3D%3D","XWFIPjYx1na9Hd5zqvq9cg%3D%3D","cwk3UgOPwlTI8aL3PRS10Q%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}